# AgroRAG Uganda 🌾

AgroRAG Uganda is a RAG-based AI assistant designed to answer agricultural questions using local Ugandan knowledge sources. Instead of relying only on a general-purpose language model, the system retrieves relevant passages from a curated document collection and uses them to produce grounded, context-aware responses.

## Purpose

The project is intended to make agricultural information easier to find and understand for:
- smallholder and commercial farmers
- agricultural students and researchers
- extension workers and local advisers
- policymakers and development partners

## What It Does

AgroRAG Uganda combines document retrieval with text generation:
1. A user asks a question in natural language.
2. The system searches a local knowledge base of Ugandan agricultural materials.
3. Relevant excerpts are passed to a language model.
4. The model generates an answer grounded in the retrieved context.

## Knowledge Base

The document collection can include:
- MAAIF reports and policy documents
- NARO research outputs and technical guides
- district agriculture office materials
- NGO and development partner reports
- extension manuals, PDFs, and DOCX files

## System Overview

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    U[User question] --> S[Streamlit interface]
    S --> R[Document retriever]
    R --> K[Ugandan agricultural knowledge base]
    R --> L[Open-source language model]
    L --> A[Context-grounded answer]
    A --> S